A||||7||Punkndrublic||Rough idle
Z||000000||Punkndrublic||06-12-99||07:14 PM||||I have an 85 GT and after the engine warms up my idle is erratic, it bounces around 650-1000 rpms. Sometimes its fine and sometimes it goes nutz, then its fine again. It happens in all different types of weather. I ve heard of ppl having this prb and wondering what it might be. The tps and map sensors are new, and i haven't checked out the iac valve yet mainly because im not sure how to test it if its testable, besides i couldn't get this part at wholesale and was reluctant to buy one.
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||06-14-99||10:15 AM||||Did you check/replace the tach-filter?
Z||000002||Carrolles||06-14-99||10:36 AM||||Check the EGR tube first.  They always crack and cause the funny idle.  You can do a simple check by spraying WD-40 on the tube while the engine is running.  If it is cracked the idle will rise when sprayed.<br>This happens because the engine is getting unmetered air.  The air gets sucked in through the EGR tube crack which is downstream of the throttle body.  The ECM compensates for the lean mixture by dumping more fuel, hence the high idle.
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||06-14-99||04:48 PM||||Yeah, that would've been my second advice... ;)<br>
Z||000004||Punkndrublic||06-14-99||08:06 PM||||Thanks for the help, i didn't think that the tach filter would affect the idle at all, but ill replace it just to make sure. I was thinking of replacing the EGR tube with a fexible stainless steel one anyways and I ve heard ppl talk about them but so does anyone know where I can get one??
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||06-15-99||12:46 AM||||A bad tachfilter causes RPM to <i>drop</i>, while a bad EGR tube causes RPM to <i>raise</i>. The tachfilter is directly connected to the ignition module. If it is bad, it draws to much current from the ignition module which can result in all kinds of problems; misfires, RPM drops, unable to start, etc.
Z||000006||PaUL||06-15-99||10:32 AM||||One way to test the tach filter would be to disconnect the tach wire from the coil then try and run it. If it still idles rough then it cant be the tach filter, if it does'nt then it must be the problem.
Z||000007||Punkndrublic||06-15-99||07:12 PM||||Ahhh I see it all makes sence now. Thanks alot, I go and check it out... when I the time    :-)
